    "Scarcity": {"Explanation": "The email does not explicitly create a sense of scarcity through limited time, quantity, or opportunity. It mentions being able to send items 'legally' and 'direct to your door,' but does not imply a shortage or urgency."},
    "Authority": {"Explanation": "There is no indication of authority or credibility from a recognized institution, title, or role. The sender identifies themselves as 'Smokers United,' but there is no reference to any authority figure or reputable organization."},
    "Commitment/Consistency": {"Explanation": "The email does not reference prior behavior or choices to push for further action. It instead provides a new offer and asks for a new action (clicking a link)."},
    "Liking": {"Explanation": "The email does not use familiarity, flattery, or personalization to build trust or rapport. It addresses the recipient formally and does not engage in any personalized communication that would build liking."},
    "Social proof": {"Explanation": "The email does not reference other people's participation or endorsement. It focuses on the benefits of the product and the discount without mentioning any social proof or testimonials from others."}
}

